---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
// Mirrors the terms text inside the app. Update both together.
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and disclaimer"
  description="Terms of use and disclaimer for GitaVerse: free for personal study, open source under GPL v3, and a note that word meanings may contain mistakes."
>
  <main id="main">
    <PageHead
      title="Terms and disclaimer"
      lead="Last updated 5 November 2026."
    />
    <section class="light">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <p>
          By using GitaVerse you agree to the points below. Please read them
          once.
        </p>
        <h2>Using the app</h2>
        <p>
          GitaVerse is free for personal reading, study and reflection. Please
          do not copy the content of the app in bulk or sell it.
        </p>
        <h2>About the text</h2>
        <p>
          The Sanskrit verses are ancient, but the transliteration, translations
          and word meanings are the work of their authors, named on the <a
            href="/credits">credits page</a
          >. A translation is an interpretation and can differ from another
          translator’s. For serious study, please read the original text with a
          teacher you trust.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          The word-by-word meanings and the glossary were written with an AI
          assistant and may contain mistakes. Check them against a trusted
          teacher or edition before relying on them for serious study.
        </div>
        <h2>Not advice</h2>
        <p>
          The app is for reading and reflection. It is not medical, legal,
          financial or mental-health advice.
        </p>
        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The app is provided as it is, without promises of any kind. We work to
          keep it correct and running, but cannot promise that it is free of
          mistakes.
        </p>
        <h2>Licences</h2>
        <p>
          The code of the app is open source under the <a href={SITE.source}
            >GNU General Public License v3.0 or later</a
          >. The fonts, libraries and verse text have their own licences, shown
          on the credits page. The GitaVerse name and logo are the author’s own
          artwork.
        </p>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.mail}`}>{SITE.mail}</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
